 "result": "`tessel routes` is implemented by `routes_command` in `src/tessel/cli.py:1047-1106`. It's registered on the `tessel` group via `TesselGroup.__init__`.\n\n**Sorting:**\n- `--sort/-s` takes `endpoint` (default), `methods`, `domain`, `rule` or `match`.\n- The first four sort the table rows with `rows.sort(key=itemgetter(sorts.index(sort)))`, so it's a plain string sort on that column.\n- `domain` only exists as a column when some rule has a host or subdomain. Otherwise `sorts.index(\"domain\")` raises `ValueError`, which is caught, and the rows stay unsorted.\n- `match` isn't in the `sorts` list either, so it hits the same `ValueError` and leaves the rows in `url_map.iter_rules()` order. That's the order Tessel matches routes when dispatching.\n\nHEAD and OPTIONS are hidden from the methods column unless `--all-methods` is passed.",
